        <mxCell id="title" value="Northeastern Marketplace — EER Diagram (v2.1)" style="text;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=22;fontStyle=1;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="40" y="35" width="1040" height="50" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="notes" value="&lt;b&gt;Rules (v1)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Sign-up requires a verified @northeastern.edu email (6-digit code). Emails are stored lowercase and the domain must match exactly.&lt;br&gt;• Boston only: Meetup Spot holds a fixed list of Boston-area spots and every item names one. To expand later, add a campus attribute to Meetup Spot.&lt;br&gt;• No in-app payment: prices are listing info, and money changes hands in person.&lt;br&gt;• Only completed transactions can be reviewed, one review per side (hence 0..2). A report targets at least one of: an item, a transaction, a user.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Value lists&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Item.category: textbooks, electronics, furniture, kitchen, clothing, dorm_essentials, sports_outdoors, bikes_transport, other&lt;br&gt;• Item.condition: new, like_new, good, fair &amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp; Item.status: available, reserved, rented_out, sold, removed&lt;br&gt;• Transaction.status: requested, accepted, declined, handed_over, returned (rentals only), completed, cancelled&lt;br&gt;• Rental.return_condition: as_lent, minor_wear, damaged &amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp; Report.status: open, in_review, resolved&lt;br&gt;• User.role: student, admin &amp;nbsp;·&amp;nbsp; User.account_status: active, suspended, deactivated&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Implementation (Supabase)&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• nu_email and email_verified_at live in Supabase Auth (auth.users); the rest of User is the profiles table.&lt;br&gt;• Text-to-SQL runs only on read-only views in a separate nlq schema, never on these tables directly.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;b&gt;Notation&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Underlined = key attribute. Cardinality is look-across: User 1..1 — Lists — 0..M Item means a user lists 0..M items and each item has exactly one owner.&lt;br&gt;• o = overlapping specialization: an item can be buyable, borrowable, or both; the double line means every item is at least one. Rental is a Transaction with type = 'rental'." style="rounded=1;arcSize=3;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=12;spacingRight=10;spacingTop=6;fillColor=#F5F5F5;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=12;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="2550" y="75" width="880" height="460" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
